<title>CHILE: Chile power co Guacolda, Candelaria pit sign deal.</title>
<headline>Chile power co Guacolda, Candelaria pit sign deal.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean electricity company Guacolda said it has signed a 10-year contract to supply power to Phelps Dodge's Candelaria copper mine in northern Chile.</p>
<p>Candelaria, which is planning a major expansion of its pit, will consume 520 million kilowatt hours a year, said the statement.</p>
<p>Guacolda is 50 percent owned by Chilgener, Chile's second largest power generating company.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
</text>
